        <item>
            <title>2.29.0</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 17:50:12 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>113</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.29.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features

- **Rebuilt the launch screen as a composer.** A wrapping row of context chips — folder, branch, worktree, machine, new-or-continue — sits above a single prompt box that holds the model, effort and permission controls. The old recent-folder and session-history lists are gone; the sidebar already lists both, and what was worth keeping moved into the chip it belongs to.
- **A new worktree gets its name from your first prompt.** Type what the session is for and the branch is named from it — `fix-issue-113` rather than `work-<timestamp>`. The prompt is optional: leave it empty and the worktree opens with nothing sent.
- **The first prompt is submitted as the session's opening turn**, so the session starts working the moment it appears.
- **New worktrees are seeded with the gitignored files a build needs** — copied with APFS clones, so a multi-gigabyte build directory costs seconds and almost no disk. A Settings toggle turns it off.
- **New worktrees branch from the repository's default branch**, not from whatever the root checkout happens to have on HEAD.
- **A session can be renamed from its pane header** by double-clicking it, alongside the sidebar's Rename item.

### Changes

- **Session titles and worktree branch names are generated ~7× faster**, going straight to the API instead of booting the CLI for a one-line answer.
- Sessions launched over SSH remote now resume by name, and the launcher's "Continue session" list for a remote host is read from that host.

### Bug Fixes

- **Fixed sessions failing to open at all with recent Claude Code extension versions.** The pane flashed and dropped back to the launcher with nothing explaining why; the launcher now names the failure when a session can't start.
- Fixed "Continue session" silently starting a fresh conversation on SSH remote hosts.
- Fixed Canopy's own SSH remote sessions being recorded on the remote machine as automated runs, which hid them from that machine's session history.
- **Fixed Sparkle silently refusing every update in the feed.** The appcast signed a rebuilt copy of the DMG rather than the one actually published, so update checks discarded the newest release and offered an older one — with no error shown. Every published entry has been re-signed.
- Fixed releases aborting when Apple's timestamp service is briefly unavailable.
]]></description>
